      "body": "Fixes #40076\n\nThis PR fixes an issue where requesting a `top_logprobs` value greater than the vocabulary size causes the server scheduler to crash with a `RuntimeError: selected index k out of range` during `topk` computation.\n\nThe fix safely bounds the requested `max_k` to the vocabulary size in both `get_top_logprobs_raw` and `get_top_logprobs_chunk` within `logprob_processor.py`.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #35311228123](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35311228123)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #35311227973](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35311227973)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #35311228120](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35311228120)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
